  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Nissan Murano?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. The Telemetry API returns fuel level as a percentage and in liters when you query with a Vehicle JWT. The segments query can also detect refuel events."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Nissan Murano with no connected services?",
      "a": "Plug in a DIMO device, which supplies the vehicle's signals with no OEM connected service. The owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, you exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT, and you read signals from the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Nissan Murano?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device, which reports a DTC event along with the DTC list and DTC count signals. Use the Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks) to have DIMO send a POST request to your targetURL when a condition you configure is met."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Nissan Murano?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device and query segments with the idling detection mechanism. It finds contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range, and maxIdleRpm lets you adjust the upper bound (default 1000)."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Nissan Murano mileage?",
      "a": "A DIMO device reports the odometer signal. To get verifiable proof, call the Attestation API's odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the resulting credential through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Nissan Murano, the vehicle connects through a DIMO device, with model years 2009 and newer. This coverage has been tested, not just expected. After the owner shares the vehicle with you, authenticate with a Developer JWT, exchange it for a Vehicle JWT, and query the Telemetry API with GraphQL."
}
